      "raw": "<p>Outstanding - curiosity about this had been killing me!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So, here&#39;s what I caught as new information beyond what we saw in the old thread:</p><ul><li><p dir=\"ltr\" id=\"docs-internal-guid-8c2a0f7a-1f32-65bb-7ed0-3c408b5a500f\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.666666666666666px;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;\">They have embraced the rule that you can use Kickers of a different color for a Minor/Major Cost.</span></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.666666666666666px;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;\">Science is now a Power, not a Quality.&nbsp; Tachyon added &quot;Physics&quot; to take its place as her d12 Quality, but Unity got some stranger changes - she has no Science, but did add Banter and Creativity.&nbsp; Guys... I think Unity might be neglecting the more formal duties of her internship.</span></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\">On the plus side, &quot;Technopath&quot; gets called out as a Power in addition to Ferrokinesis.</p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.666666666666666px;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;\">It may no longer be possible to take Defense as a reaction by taking a Minor Cost.&nbsp; The possibility is never mentioned.</span></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.666666666666666px;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;\">The Megalopolis Stress Track was 12 boxes, 4 of each color. &nbsp;What we had before on Environment Stress was 3G-XY-3R, so it seems like more Green and Red boxes are on the table.</span></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.666666666666666px;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;\">The GM allowed Create A Bonus to be split among multiple recipients. &nbsp;This did not appear to be official.</span></p></li></ul>",
