      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-27T21:16:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Good times.&nbsp; The new information here is a little more subtle than last time, but there's some good stuff to find:</p><ul>\n<li>Using a back issue to max out a die is a choice you make after rolling.&nbsp; It would appear that it also means you use your Max die for the action, even if you would otherwise use your Min die - that's a BIG buff.</li>\n<li>Also, I don't recall hearing previously what a big deal it is to roll triples - you get a Spotlight Moment and an automatic success.</li>\n<li>It's the PCs, not the GM, who decides whether the Minor/Major Costs are paid as Hero Costs or Environment Costs, subject to things making narrative sense.</li>\n</ul>",
