      "id": 163551,
      "name": "Ironic",
      "username": "Ironic",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-28T01:25:52.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Chrono\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chrono/48/2334_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chrono:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I believe they do talk about stress recovery in the other thread.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not in detail.&nbsp; Most of the things from the back side of the Cheat Sheet remain shrouded in mystery, and the sum total of what was said about Recovery was:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Animus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/animus/48/1887_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Animus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There was mention of Recovery rules, and a certain level of success healing you up to the minimum of the next category up. E.g., if Legacy is down to 17 stress (yellow), a complete success (8-11) would heal him up to 25 (minimum stress for green). Other than that, I don't remember anything.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>…and that's it.&nbsp; The other things back there were apparently Principles, rolling triples, and callbacks, all of which we've learned a little more about over time.</p>\n<p>It being an action between scenes does add further context, though!&nbsp; In particular, it makes it clear what a huge deal it can be that Absolute Zero (according to the sheet we've seen, at least) can get up to his low Green level from any Stress.&nbsp; It also makes me wonder whether Bunker's Recharge Mode is any different now, or if it allows Recovery actions in combat, or what.</p>\n<p>Also, for anyone who wasn't there or needs a refresher, <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/sentinels-rpg-7316\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">this</a> is the page I'm getting most of my RPG info from.&nbsp; Well, it and the assorted links it contains, most notably <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/BbYWY\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">this one</a>.</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:44:35.881Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
