      "raw": "[quote=\"Chrono\"]\nI believe they do talk about stress recovery in the other thread.\n[/quote]\nNot in detail.&nbsp; Most of the things from the back side of the Cheat Sheet remain shrouded in mystery, and the sum total of what was said about Recovery was:\n\n[quote=\"Animus\"]\nThere was mention of Recovery rules, and a certain level of success healing you up to the minimum of the next category up. E.g., if Legacy is down to 17 stress (yellow), a complete success (8-11) would heal him up to 25 (minimum stress for green). Other than that, I don&#39;t remember anything.\n[/quote]\n...and that&#39;s it.&nbsp; The other things back there were apparently Principles, rolling triples, and callbacks, all of which we&#39;ve learned a little more about over time.\n\nIt being an action between scenes does add further context, though!&nbsp; In particular, it makes it clear what a huge deal it can be that Absolute Zero (according to the sheet we&#39;ve seen, at least) can get up to his low Green level from any Stress.&nbsp; It also makes me wonder whether Bunker&#39;s Recharge Mode is any different now, or if it allows Recovery actions in combat, or what.\n\nAlso, for anyone who wasn&#39;t there or needs a refresher, <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/sentinels-rpg-7316\">this</a> is the page I&#39;m getting most of my RPG info from.&nbsp; Well, it and the assorted links it contains, most notably <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/BbYWY\">this one</a>.\n",
