    {
      "id": 163553,
      "name": "Ironic",
      "username": "Ironic",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-28T03:42:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hurm.&nbsp; So that sounds something like:</p><ul>\n<li>1-3: Bottom of the next level up.</li>\n<li>4-7: Top of the next level up.</li>\n<li>8-10: All Stress recovered.</li>\n<li>12+: Full recovery, plus some extra benefit?</li>\n</ul><p>Interesting, even though I've surely made some mistakes here.&nbsp; Thanks for the hints!</p><p>EDIT: Oh, hey, the third part is up!&nbsp; Sadly, Ambuscade went down too fast to give much of an exhibition on how named villains work.&nbsp; He did show something interesting, though - every Hero we've seen has the same Stress as their HP in the card game, but he didn't take anything like 50 damage to get there.&nbsp; (I suspect he had 25 Stress - I counted him taking 27 points, but may have missed a few.&nbsp; However much he did take, it was more than needed.)</p><p>I am interested to know that marking Costs makes it harder for it to be your Backissue.&nbsp; That surprises me a little (aren't the heroes put through the narrative wringer the hardest usually the MOST central ones, in games as well as comics?), but critiquing the advancement mechanics of a Beta is a bit silly, even for me.</p><p>Thanks again for posting all of these!</p>",
      "post_number": 13,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:44:36.015Z",
