      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Hurm.&nbsp; So that sounds something like:</p><ul><li>1-3: Bottom of the next level up.</li><li>4-7: Top of the next level up.</li><li>8-10: All Stress recovered.</li><li>12+: Full recovery, plus some extra benefit?</li></ul><p>Interesting, even though I&#39;ve surely made some mistakes here.&nbsp; Thanks for the hints!</p><p>EDIT: Oh, hey, the third part is up!&nbsp; Sadly, Ambuscade went down too fast to give much of an exhibition on how named villains work.&nbsp; He did show something interesting, though - every Hero we&#39;ve seen has the same Stress as their HP in the card game, but he didn&#39;t take anything like 50 damage to get there.&nbsp; (I suspect he had 25 Stress - I counted him taking 27 points, but may have missed a few.&nbsp; However much he did take, it was more than needed.)</p><p>I am interested to know that marking Costs makes it harder for it to be your Backissue.&nbsp; That surprises me a little (aren&#39;t the heroes put through the narrative wringer the hardest usually the MOST central ones, in games as well as comics?), but critiquing the advancement mechanics of a Beta is a bit silly, even for me.</p><p>Thanks again for posting all of these!</p>",
